to-be-incorporated-into-paper-lines-11 : List (List Word)
to-be-incorporated-into-paper-lines-11 = cons "- **The root: data without meaning.** A file is bytes with a name; what it means is held by" (cons "  whatever program reads it. So whoever owns the program owns the meaning of the data, and every" (cons "  wall in computing is that ownership: formats (agreements between programs about meaningless" (cons "  bytes), applications (code with private storage and a fixed screen), APIs (holes a company cuts" (cons "  into its storage on its terms), copy-paste (the one operation that crosses everything, because it" (cons "  carries text and drops meaning), accounts (identity held by a provider), sync conflicts reported as" (cons "  errors, updates that change what runs without the owner, the source/binary split (what runs cannot" (cons "  be read or changed by whoever runs it), and the user/programmer split. In hyperactivity data is a" (cons "  term with its type, so its meaning travels with it and no program holds it." nil))))))))
